From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NotAlexNoyle <alexnoyle@icloud.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 03:21:16 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] gpu compositor: the frame's paint and its compose posted
 apart; compose jobs from any thread

T-515, frames made off the main thread. JihadComposeStart was the layer paint (main thread) and the
compose job's post in one call. They are now apart: jihad_offscreen_paint_layers(widget, docshell)
flushes and paints the layers, as Start does first; jihad_offscreen_compose_post(...) posts the
compose and read of the layer tree as it stands, from any thread, at a view and scroll it is given
(or the ones last set). The daemon's express lane posts its frames from a thread of its own while
the main thread runs the page's script or a layer paint.

The job list is shared with that thread, so it is under a mutex: start, post, forget and abandon
take it; a poll without a wait holds it for the whole poll (a forget between the find and the
job's monitor would let the compositor task free the job under it). jihad_offscreen_compose_peek
reads a job's state without taking its result (1 done, 2 composed and being read, 0 pending).
A forgotten job's cancelled flag was set even when the job was done; it is set only with abandoned.
